1
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:11,070
Brace the wind.

2
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:16,520
The lord of light has made good on his promise, my king.

3
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:19,040
His fires have melted the snows away.

4
00:02:19,550 --> 00:02:21,160
The way ahead is clear.

5
00:02:21,160 --> 00:02:22,740
We ride for Winterfell.

6
00:02:22,830 --> 00:02:24,380
And you will take it.

7
00:02:25,810 --> 00:02:28,880
The lord has shown me Bolton Banners burning.

8
00:02:29,110 --> 00:02:31,850
You will receive what is yours by right.

9
00:02:53,030 --> 00:02:54,050
Your grace.

10
00:02:54,740 --> 00:02:56,130
Prepare to form up.

11
00:02:56,130 --> 00:02:57,140
Your grace.

12
00:03:01,490 --> 00:03:02,470
Tell me.

13
00:03:02,620 --> 00:03:06,320
The men, many deserted before dawn.

14
00:03:08,810 --> 00:03:09,930
How many?

15
00:03:10,520 --> 00:03:11,850
Nearly half.

16
00:03:12,670 --> 00:03:15,440
All the sellswords with all the horses.

17
00:03:26,430 --> 00:03:27,350
Your grace.

18
00:03:30,160 --> 00:03:33,150
Speak up. Can't be worse than mutiny.

19
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:05,520
Cut her down.

20
00:04:19,200 --> 00:04:20,240
Your grace.

21
00:04:20,990 --> 00:04:24,040
The lady Melisandre was just seen riding out of camp.

22
00:04:36,550 --> 00:04:38,720
Get the men into marching formation.

23
00:04:40,490 --> 00:04:42,060
On to Winterfell.

24
00:04:47,100 --> 00:04:48,560
He raised his hands

25
00:04:50,370 --> 00:04:52,170
and they all stood up at once.

26
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:58,180
Tens of thousands of them. The biggest army in the world.

27
00:04:58,860 --> 00:05:00,300
So what are you gonna do?

28
00:05:03,490 --> 00:05:06,090
I'm gonna hope they don't learn how to climb the Wall.

29
00:05:06,760 --> 00:05:09,550
But the dragonglass...

30
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:12,730
No one's ever getting that back now.

31
00:05:13,330 --> 00:05:14,960
It wouldn't have mattered anyway.

32
00:05:14,960 --> 00:05:16,490
Not unless we had a mountain of it.

33
00:05:16,490 --> 00:05:19,320
But you killed a white walker.

34
00:05:19,320 --> 00:05:20,770
With Longclaw.

35
00:05:22,080 --> 00:05:24,530
I saw them shatter steel axes like they were glass.

36
00:05:24,530 --> 00:05:27,500
- But Longclaw... - is Valyrian steel.

37
00:05:27,500 --> 00:05:30,240
How many Valyrian steel swords are left in the Seven Kingdoms?

38
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:31,540
Not enough.

39
00:05:34,430 --> 00:05:37,660
The first Lord Commander in history to sacrifice

40
00:05:37,670 --> 00:05:40,470
the lives of sworn brothers to save the lives of wildlings.

41
00:05:44,070 --> 00:05:47,460
How's it feel to be friends with the most hated man in Castle Black?

42
00:05:47,460 --> 00:05:49,600
You were friends with me when I first came here.

43
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:51,880
And I wasn't winning any elections back then.

44
00:05:51,880 --> 00:05:53,390
Here's to us, then.

45
00:05:54,620 --> 00:05:56,200
Long may they sneer.

46
00:06:04,590 --> 00:06:05,590
What?

47
00:06:08,810 --> 00:06:10,470
I wanted to ask you something.

48
00:06:12,110 --> 00:06:14,010
To ask something of you.

49
00:06:16,970 --> 00:06:20,240
Send me, Gilly, and the baby to Oldtown

50
00:06:20,240 --> 00:06:21,900
so I can become a maester.

51
00:06:22,680 --> 00:06:25,030
That's what I'm meant to be. Not this.

52
00:06:25,030 --> 00:06:26,990
I need you here, Sam.

53
00:06:28,040 --> 00:06:30,690
If you leave, who's left to give me advice I trust?

54
00:06:31,840 --> 00:06:33,370
Well, there's Edd.

55
00:06:36,970 --> 00:06:39,170
I'd be more use to you as a maester.

56
00:06:39,660 --> 00:06:42,310
More use to everyone now that Maester Aemon is gone.

57
00:06:43,450 --> 00:06:46,100
The Citadel has the world's greatest library.

58
00:06:46,640 --> 00:06:49,510
I'll learn about history,

59
00:06:49,510 --> 00:06:51,430
strategy, healing.

60
00:06:52,090 --> 00:06:53,620
And other things,

61
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:55,680
things that will help when--

62
00:06:57,070 --> 00:06:58,400
when they come.

63
00:07:01,510 --> 00:07:03,730
If Gilly stays here, then she'll die.

64
00:07:05,320 --> 00:07:08,070
And the baby that she named after me will die.

65
00:07:09,030 --> 00:07:11,960
And I'll end up dying, too, trying to protect them.

66
00:07:14,520 --> 00:07:17,050
Which means that the last thing that I'll see in this world

67
00:07:17,460 --> 00:07:20,030
will be the look in her eyes when I fail them.

68
00:07:24,790 --> 00:07:27,730
And I'd rather see a thousand white walkers than see that.

69
00:07:42,850 --> 00:07:44,200
Thank you.

70
00:07:46,010 --> 00:07:48,580
You know that the Citadel will make you swear off women, too.

71
00:07:48,580 --> 00:07:50,440
Oh, they'll bloody try.

72
00:07:54,230 --> 00:07:56,950
- Sam. - What?

73
00:07:58,360 --> 00:07:59,510
Sam.

74
00:08:01,810 --> 00:08:04,060
You had just been beaten half to death. How did you--

75
00:08:04,110 --> 00:08:05,880
Oh, very carefully.

76
00:08:08,690 --> 00:08:11,470
I'm glad the end of the world's working out well for someone.

77
00:08:16,680 --> 00:08:18,140
I'll come back.

78
00:08:20,160 --> 00:08:21,500
To your return.

79
00:08:22,580 --> 00:08:23,790
To my return.

80
00:10:03,340 --> 00:10:05,590
Aye, this way.

81
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:42,590
My lady!

82
00:10:44,790 --> 00:10:45,780
Stannis.

83
00:10:46,180 --> 00:10:48,650
Stannis Baratheon is coming. His whole army.

84
00:10:48,690 --> 00:10:49,910
How do you know it's Stannis?

85
00:10:49,910 --> 00:10:51,890
They're carrying his flaming heart banners.

86
00:10:52,180 --> 00:10:55,410
From the Blackwater. I'll never forget it.

87
00:11:32,650 --> 00:11:33,910
Trench here.

88
00:11:34,500 --> 00:11:36,710
Another one 300 yards from the castle wall.

89
00:11:36,710 --> 00:11:37,920
Hurry them along.

90
00:11:40,340 --> 00:11:41,740
Dig between those two rises.

91
00:11:41,740 --> 00:11:43,560
- Spread out. - I'm with you.

92
00:11:43,720 --> 00:11:46,030
- Archers! - Spread out!

93
00:11:46,030 --> 00:11:48,390
And send out a foraging party immediately.

94
00:11:48,390 --> 00:11:50,150
Siege begins at sunrise.

95
00:11:50,920 --> 00:11:53,530
There's not going to be a siege, Your Grace.

96
00:12:34,820 --> 00:12:36,880
We've got no chance!

97
00:13:46,810 --> 00:13:48,210
No, please, please.

98
00:14:42,790 --> 00:14:44,790
Bolton has women fighting for him?

99
00:14:46,100 --> 00:14:48,150
I don't fight for the Boltons.

100
00:14:49,580 --> 00:14:51,280
I'm Brienne of Tarth.

101
00:14:53,700 --> 00:14:56,160
I was kingsguard to Renly Baratheon.

102
00:15:02,690 --> 00:15:05,990
I was there when he was murdered by a shadow with your face.

103
00:15:09,430 --> 00:15:12,510
You murdered him with blood magic?

104
00:15:18,290 --> 00:15:19,380
I did.

105
00:15:28,900 --> 00:15:32,800
In the name of Renly of house Baratheon, first of his name,

106
00:15:33,060 --> 00:15:36,230
rightful king of the Andals and the First Men,

107
00:15:36,290 --> 00:15:39,510
Lord of the Seven Kingdoms and protector of the realm,

108
00:15:39,510 --> 00:15:43,050
I, Brienne of Tarth, sentence you to die.

109
00:15:50,110 --> 00:15:51,780
Do you have any last words?

110
00:16:01,320 --> 00:16:02,800
Go on, do your duty.

111
00:16:21,360 --> 00:16:22,860
Looks like we're done here.

112
00:16:39,200 --> 00:16:41,800
I surrender! I surrender!

113
00:16:42,050 --> 00:16:43,870
And I accept your surrender.

114
00:16:56,340 --> 00:16:57,700
Let's head back.

115
00:16:58,030 --> 00:16:59,820
My wife must be lonely.

116
00:17:33,780 --> 00:17:34,950
My lady.

117
00:17:35,220 --> 00:17:37,320
I've come to escort you back to your chamber.

118
00:17:37,580 --> 00:17:40,000
Go with her, please.

119
00:17:43,840 --> 00:17:45,540
I know what Ramsay is.

120
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:48,760
I know what he'll do to me.

121
00:17:52,200 --> 00:17:53,830
If I'm going to die,

122
00:17:54,540 --> 00:17:57,730
let it happen while there's still some of me left.

123
00:17:59,920 --> 00:18:00,940
Die?

124
00:18:02,430 --> 00:18:03,960
Who said anything about dying?

125
00:18:04,160 --> 00:18:05,470
You can't die.

126
00:18:05,610 --> 00:18:07,570
Your father was Warden of the North.

127
00:18:07,570 --> 00:18:08,940
Ramsay needs you.

128
00:18:11,920 --> 00:18:13,870
Though I suppose he doesn't need all of you.

129
00:18:15,050 --> 00:18:17,360
Just the parts he'll use to make his heir,

130
00:18:17,360 --> 00:18:20,780
until you've given him a boy or two and he's finished using them.

131
00:18:22,240 --> 00:18:27,200
Then he's got incredible plans for those parts.

132
00:18:28,480 --> 00:18:30,840
So, shall we wait for him to come back

133
00:18:30,840 --> 00:18:32,440
or should we begin now?

134
00:18:34,920 --> 00:18:36,370
You're leaving it to me?

135
00:18:37,240 --> 00:18:38,320
Good.

136
00:18:38,890 --> 00:18:40,460
Let's begin.

137
00:18:43,050 --> 00:18:44,890
Reek... stop!

138
00:18:44,890 --> 00:18:46,650
Stop!

139
00:18:54,300 --> 00:18:55,770
Open the gate!

140
00:19:03,660 --> 00:19:04,910
He's coming back.

141
00:20:40,900 --> 00:20:43,290
I can see I have my work cut out for me.

142
00:20:44,580 --> 00:20:46,530
You two, out.

143
00:21:40,790 --> 00:21:42,710
You were the first person on my list, you know.

144
00:21:44,220 --> 00:21:46,230
For killing Syrio Forel. Remember him?

145
00:21:48,220 --> 00:21:49,380
Probably not.

146
00:21:51,900 --> 00:21:53,520
I've gotten a few of the others.

147
00:21:55,230 --> 00:21:57,550
The many-faced god stole a few more from me.

148
00:21:59,020 --> 00:22:00,750
But I'm glad he left me you.

149
00:22:04,800 --> 00:22:06,320
Do you know who I am?

150
00:22:10,900 --> 00:22:12,140
I can't hear you.

151
00:22:21,620 --> 00:22:23,150
You know who I am.

152
00:22:24,230 --> 00:22:26,040
I'm Arya Stark.

153
00:22:34,900 --> 00:22:36,310
Do you know who you are?

154
00:22:39,650 --> 00:22:40,860
You're no one.

155
00:22:42,960 --> 00:22:44,240
You're nothing.

156
00:23:28,270 --> 00:23:30,200
A girl has taken a life.

157
00:23:31,310 --> 00:23:32,880
The wrong life.

158
00:23:35,030 --> 00:23:36,470
I was right about her.

159
00:23:37,400 --> 00:23:38,630
You were.

160
00:23:40,170 --> 00:23:41,400
You're not ready.

161
00:23:43,820 --> 00:23:44,990
Not at all.

162
00:23:49,300 --> 00:23:51,710
That man's life was not yours to take.

163
00:23:53,360 --> 00:23:55,680
A girl stole from the many-faced god.

164
00:23:57,090 --> 00:23:58,800
Now a debt is owed.

165
00:24:05,430 --> 00:24:07,280
Only death can pay for life.

166
00:24:20,540 --> 00:24:22,630
No! No!

167
00:24:22,630 --> 00:24:26,070
No, you... don't die! Don't die!

168
00:24:31,450 --> 00:24:32,750
Why are you crying?

169
00:24:35,280 --> 00:24:36,820
He was my friend.

170
00:24:36,920 --> 00:24:39,430
No, he wasn't. Didn't you listen to him?

171
00:24:40,880 --> 00:24:42,110
He was no one.

172
00:24:46,460 --> 00:24:47,930
But if you're...

173
00:24:50,870 --> 00:24:52,140
Who's this?

174
00:24:52,530 --> 00:24:54,000
No one at all.

175
00:24:54,600 --> 00:24:55,810
Just as a girl should have been

176
00:24:55,810 --> 00:24:57,710
before she took a face from the hall.

177
00:25:04,030 --> 00:25:05,680
The faces are for no one.

178
00:25:06,970 --> 00:25:08,620
You are still someone.

179
00:25:11,750 --> 00:25:13,020
And to someone,

180
00:25:13,260 --> 00:25:15,450
the faces are as good as poison.

181
00:25:28,510 --> 00:25:29,750
I can't see.

182
00:25:36,290 --> 00:25:37,410
What's happening?

183
00:25:39,060 --> 00:25:40,450
What's happening?!

184
00:25:51,090 --> 00:25:53,870
- I wish you a safe journey home. - Thank you.

185
00:25:59,080 --> 00:26:00,410
Forgive me, child.

186
00:26:02,550 --> 00:26:05,040
I wish you all the happiness in the world.

187
00:26:22,630 --> 00:26:24,540
Maybe I'll come visit you sometime.

188
00:26:25,190 --> 00:26:26,730
Maybe I'll come visit you.

189
00:26:26,870 --> 00:26:28,210
Don't wait too long.

190
00:26:28,390 --> 00:26:30,500
Got a noblewoman to marry back home.

191
00:26:31,400 --> 00:26:32,900
You want a good girl,

192
00:26:32,950 --> 00:26:34,970
but you need the bad pussy.

193
00:26:38,660 --> 00:26:40,210
Whenever you're ready, my lord.

194
00:26:56,850 --> 00:26:58,550
Try not to lose it this time.

195
00:27:00,890 --> 00:27:02,420
I'll never take it off again.

196
00:27:03,810 --> 00:27:05,580
I know you didn't want to leave Dorne,

197
00:27:06,680 --> 00:27:08,500
but I'm glad you're coming home.

198
00:27:09,030 --> 00:27:11,030
Your mother's desperate to see you.

199
00:27:11,040 --> 00:27:13,020
I'm glad Trystane is coming with us.

200
00:27:13,020 --> 00:27:14,570
He seems like a nice boy.

201
00:27:15,450 --> 00:27:16,780
You're lucky.

202
00:27:16,960 --> 00:27:19,250
Arranged marriages are rarely so--

203
00:27:20,280 --> 00:27:22,090
so well arranged.

204
00:27:22,090 --> 00:27:23,840
Do you think mother will like him?

205
00:27:25,040 --> 00:27:28,750
If she sees you're happy, I'm sure she will.

206
00:27:28,840 --> 00:27:30,460
You really believe that?

207
00:27:31,130 --> 00:27:33,010
Have you ever known your mother to like anyone

208
00:27:33,010 --> 00:27:34,710
aside from her children?

209
00:27:35,550 --> 00:27:37,180
She likes you.

210
00:27:37,510 --> 00:27:39,470
I'm not so sure about that.

211
00:27:40,260 --> 00:27:41,290
Listen...

212
00:27:43,830 --> 00:27:45,690
There's something I wanted to tell you.

213
00:27:47,260 --> 00:27:49,370
Something I should have told you long ago.

214
00:27:50,670 --> 00:27:51,690
So...

215
00:27:54,520 --> 00:27:56,540
Now that you've seen more of the world,

216
00:27:57,120 --> 00:28:01,010
you've learned how complicated things can be,

217
00:28:01,010 --> 00:28:02,560
people can be.

218
00:28:03,210 --> 00:28:06,450
The Lannisters and the Martells have hated each other for years,

219
00:28:06,450 --> 00:28:08,640
but you've fallen in love with Trystane.

220
00:28:08,640 --> 00:28:11,290
It was an accident, really. I mean, what were the chances?

221
00:28:11,400 --> 00:28:13,080
You happen to fall in love with the man

222
00:28:13,090 --> 00:28:15,270
you were assigned to marry?

223
00:28:15,800 --> 00:28:17,010
My point is...

224
00:28:19,340 --> 00:28:21,620
We don't choose whom we love.

225
00:28:22,340 --> 00:28:24,630
It just, well--

226
00:28:26,920 --> 00:28:29,160
It's beyond our control.

227
00:28:29,160 --> 00:28:31,140
- I sound like an idiot. - No, you don't.

228
00:28:31,140 --> 00:28:33,740
What I'm trying to say-- what I'm trying

229
00:28:33,740 --> 00:28:35,050
and failing to say--

230
00:28:35,050 --> 00:28:36,390
I know what you're trying to say.

231
00:28:36,390 --> 00:28:38,510
No, I'm afraid you don't.

232
00:28:39,330 --> 00:28:40,440
I do.

233
00:28:43,940 --> 00:28:45,020
I know.

234
00:28:46,800 --> 00:28:48,060
About you and mother.

235
00:28:50,510 --> 00:28:52,740
I think a part of me always knew.

236
00:28:54,750 --> 00:28:57,690
And I'm glad.

237
00:29:00,770 --> 00:29:03,020
I'm glad that you're my father.

238
00:29:38,300 --> 00:29:39,320
Myrcella?

239
00:29:43,080 --> 00:29:44,150
Myrcella?

240
00:29:51,200 --> 00:29:53,870
Myrcella? Myrcella?

241
00:31:12,450 --> 00:31:13,980
You love her, don't you?

242
00:31:18,420 --> 00:31:19,660
How could you not?

243
00:31:20,750 --> 00:31:23,020
Of course it's hopeless for the both of you.

244
00:31:23,960 --> 00:31:27,190
A sellsword from the fighting pits, a disgraced knight.

245
00:31:27,660 --> 00:31:29,820
Neither one of you is fit consort for a queen.

246
00:31:31,770 --> 00:31:35,390
But we always want the wrong woman.

247
00:31:36,440 --> 00:31:37,930
Does he always talk so much?

248
00:31:41,990 --> 00:31:43,430
Jorah the Andal.

249
00:31:44,130 --> 00:31:45,340
Torgo Nudho.

250
00:31:45,340 --> 00:31:46,860
He should not be here.

251
00:31:47,060 --> 00:31:48,370
No, but he is.

252
00:31:48,370 --> 00:31:50,920
Our queen ordered him exiled from city.

253
00:31:50,920 --> 00:31:53,420
Our queen would be dead if not for him.

254
00:32:15,930 --> 00:32:18,530
Punila. Thank you.

255
00:32:19,290 --> 00:32:20,450
I am sorry.

256
00:32:21,330 --> 00:32:24,210
Sorry I not there to fight for our queen.

257
00:32:24,210 --> 00:32:25,500
You missed a good scrap.

258
00:32:25,500 --> 00:32:26,730
None of that matters now.

259
00:32:26,730 --> 00:32:28,550
The longer we sit here bantering,

260
00:32:28,550 --> 00:32:31,110
the longer Daenerys is out there in the wilderness.

261
00:32:31,140 --> 00:32:33,490
He's right. The dragon headed north.

262
00:32:33,490 --> 00:32:35,430
If we're going to find her, that's where we'll have to go.

263
00:32:35,440 --> 00:32:36,560
We?

264
00:32:37,250 --> 00:32:38,590
You're a Lannister.

265
00:32:38,690 --> 00:32:41,330
The queen intends to remove your family from power.

266
00:32:41,330 --> 00:32:43,170
And I intend to help her do it.

267
00:32:43,170 --> 00:32:45,250
You've been here for how many days now?

268
00:32:45,410 --> 00:32:47,310
I've fought for her for years.

269
00:32:47,560 --> 00:32:49,290
Since she was little more than a child.

270
00:32:49,290 --> 00:32:51,180
- You betrayed her. - Careful now.

271
00:32:51,190 --> 00:32:53,760
And she exiled you. Twice, I believe.

272
00:32:53,760 --> 00:32:55,290
The second time thanks to you.

273
00:32:55,290 --> 00:32:57,850
Don't blame me for your crimes, Mormont.

274
00:32:57,850 --> 00:33:00,680
He's right. Our queen exiled Jorah.

275
00:33:00,680 --> 00:33:03,030
And he's right. Jorah saved her life.

276
00:33:03,500 --> 00:33:05,640
Perhaps she feels differently about him now.

277
00:33:05,640 --> 00:33:08,820
Perhaps not. The only way we'll know is if we ask her.

278
00:33:09,170 --> 00:33:11,690
Fine, fine. I suppose he can join us.

279
00:33:11,690 --> 00:33:14,530
Just as long as he promises not to kill me in my sleep.

280
00:33:14,530 --> 00:33:17,550
If I ever kill you, your eyes will be wide open.

281
00:33:17,550 --> 00:33:20,450
Forgive me, but why would we bring you?

282
00:33:22,490 --> 00:33:25,380
- Pardon me? - Have you ever tracked animals in the wilderness?

283
00:33:25,610 --> 00:33:28,300
Not precisely, but I have other skills that would be useful.

284
00:33:28,300 --> 00:33:29,520
Can you fight?

285
